"Autumn came to Wildhaven the way everything came to Wildhaven — completely, and without asking a screen for permission.",
"Kai stood on the dormitory roof at dusk, Scout on his shoulder, watching the valley put itself to bed. He'd been a keeper-in-training for one season. His Attention Score, wherever it lived now in some patient database, was presumably in ruins. His actual attention was the strongest it had ever been: he could hear rain coming, name forty critters by their verse in the song, sit still for a whole hour and come back richer.",
"He was also, though he wouldn't learn the details for another year, mildly famous: the boy-shaped blur in seven million people's minute-and-forty-seconds. Somewhere in Meridian, kids had started a game of taking their Lenses off and staring at fences, just in case. Somewhere in the Spire, a warm voice was very carefully not filing certain reports, and a woman with a whip-smart daughter was reading anomaly logs late into the night, getting closer. Somewhere under all of it, his grandmother was a splinter in the heart of the machine, waiting.",
"The swarm was coming. Maro said it. Vex planned for it. The song, on quiet nights, braced for it.",
"But that was Book Two's problem.",
